## Iteration 8 — 2026-10-02 22:56
Item 07 (Bonds, groups, concept mappings): **SO

Item 07 (bonds, groups, concept mappings) is done and the gate passes (451 Racket tests plus the Chez checks). `chez_scheme/original/` is untouched, and nothing is committed.

**What was ported**
- `bonds.ss`, `groups.ss` and `concept-mappings.ss` are now `racket/engine/*.rktl`, included in the original load order. Apart from the headers they are copied verbatim, with one exception, explained below.
- `group-graphics` is now in the engine too (`racket/engine/group-graphics.rktl`). `groups.ss` calls it even with graphics off, so a headless run needs it. It only sends messages to the Workspace window.

**The test harness**
- `tests/diff/codelet-harness.scm` is a copy of the original's run loop with only the 10 bond and group codelet types turned on. It runs under Chez with the original loaded and under Racket with the port.
- The trace has one line per codelet and one per update cycle: codelet type, urgency, random-generator state, structures built and broken, temperature, activations and Workspace objects.
- `racket/tests/codelet-diff-test.rkt` compares the two traces line by line and names the problem, seed and codelet where they first differ.
- It covers all 109 runs in `tests/problems.txt` for 400 codelets, plus 7 runs of 2000 codelets that reach the merging of sameness groups. It takes about 22 s.
- A one-off sweep outside the gate (all 109 runs × 2000 codelets) gave byte-identical traces.
- 15 of 16 deliberate edits to the ported code made the test fail. The one it missed (swapping the arguments of an `intersect`) doesn't change behaviour here.

**A real divergence, now fixed**
- In `abc abd iijjkk` seed 3, the port parted from the original after codelet 735.
- The cause: in `groups.ss`, `get-local-density` passes two arguments to `append` that both make random draws. Chez evaluates the second argument first and Racket the first.
- The fix is the one changed line in `groups.rktl`, marked `port:`. No other call in the three files has two arguments that draw.
- The 400-codelet runs never reached it; only a 2000-codelet run did. That's why the long runs are now part of the test.

**Found in the original** (logged in `docs/anomalies_and_quirks.md`)
- `bonds-equal?` calls `same-direction?`, which no file defines. Nothing calls `bonds-equal?`, so it never fails. The port's stand-in raises an error, as Chez would.
- Two group fonts are read but never defined; the Workspace window creates them at run time.

**Not covered yet**
- Concept mappings are only created through bridges, so a run with bridges off never makes one. The battery tests them directly instead: every message, for all pairs of instances of each slipnet category and for real letter and group descriptions.
- Bridge-related paths in bonds and groups wait for item 08.
- The golden traces can't be compared yet: real runs post bridge scouts from the very first codelets.

PROGRESS.md has the details and notes for item 08.

# result: success in 1550s, 96 turns, cost $5.44
